{:edb/db-before-t 1693 :edb/db-after-t 1694 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535006 50 #inst "2026-10-08T14:09:41.155Z" 13194139535006 true] [17592186326143 1017 #edb/ref 17592186326144 13194139535006 false] [17592186326143 1017 #edb/ref 17592186326270 13194139535006 true] [17592186326143 1100 "The population $P(t)$ of fish in a pond after $t$ weeks can be modeled by the differential equation ${P}^{′}(t)=0.09P(t).$ If the fish population was $8\\,000$ after $18$ weeks, calculate the fish population after $23$ weeks." 13194139535006 false] [17592186326143 1100 "The population $P(t)$ of fish in a pond after $t$ weeks can be modeled by the differential equation ${P}^{′}(t)=0.09P(t).$ If the fish population was $8\\,000$ after $18$ weeks, calculate the fish population after $23$ weeks. Round the final population to the nearest whole fish. Do not round intermediate values." 13194139535006 true] [17592186326143 1145 "The general solution to the given differential equation is\n\n$$\nP(t)={P}_{0}\\,{e}^{0.09t},\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{0}$ is the initial fish population.\n\nWe are given that after $18$ weeks, the population was $8\\,000.$ So, substituting $t=18$ and $P(18)=8\\,000$ into our general solution and solving for ${P}_{0},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(18) & ={P}_{0}\\,{e}^{0.09\\cdot 18} \\\\ 8\\,000 & ={P}_{0}\\,{e}^{1.62} \\\\ {P}_{0} & =\\frac{8\\,000}{{e}^{1.62}} \\\\  & ≈1\\,583.190,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.\n\nHence, our particular solution is\n\n$$\nP(t)=1\\,583.190\\,{e}^{0.09t}.\n$$\n\nWe want to find the fish population after $23$ weeks. So, substituting $t=23$ into our particular solution, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(23) & =1\\,583.190\\,{e}^{0.09\\cdot 23} \\\\  & =1\\,583.190\\,{e}^{2.07} \\\\  & ≈12\\,547,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest whole number. \n\nTherefore, approximately $12\\,547$ fish will be in the pond after $23$ weeks." 13194139535006 false] [17592186326143 1145 "The solution of $P'(t)=0.09P(t)$ satisfies\n\n$$P(t)=P(18)e^{0.09(t-18)}=8\\,000e^{0.09(t-18)}.$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$P(23)=8\\,000e^{0.45}\\approx12\\,546.49748392135.$$\n\nRounding only this final value to the nearest whole number gives approximately $12\\,546$ fish." 13194139535006 true] [17592186326270 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326271 13194139535006 true] [17592186326270 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326272 13194139535006 true] [17592186326270 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326273 13194139535006 true] [17592186326270 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326274 13194139535006 true] [17592186326270 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326275 13194139535006 true] [17592186326270 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535006 true] [17592186326270 1041 "selection" 13194139535006 true] [17592186326270 1104 #edb/ref 17592186326274 13194139535006 true] [17592186326270 1110 #uuid "c74c17a5-d710-5292-8240-89c348450327" 13194139535006 true] [17592186326271 1034 "14\\,257" 13194139535006 true] [17592186326271 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535006 true] [17592186326271 1111 #uuid "67a5e2e3-661b-58da-9754-38289986c43d" 13194139535006 true] [17592186326272 1034 "14\\,542" 13194139535006 true] [17592186326272 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535006 true] [17592186326272 1111 #uuid "d72f818d-b6b9-5d99-a623-f1b2198169a1" 13194139535006 true] [17592186326273 1034 "17\\,542" 13194139535006 true] [17592186326273 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535006 true] [17592186326273 1111 #uuid "57547bc3-909e-5ac8-bf79-7ec5486f0ed2" 13194139535006 true] [17592186326274 1034 "12\\,546" 13194139535006 true] [17592186326274 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535006 true] [17592186326274 1111 #uuid "ff1764e6-358f-5325-a1b8-898807f37758" 13194139535006 true] [17592186326275 1034 "15\\,247" 13194139535006 true] [17592186326275 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535006 true] [17592186326275 1111 #uuid "dd2e959c-beac-5225-89b1-d6d147a0c341" 13194139535006 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-339239/mathematical-correction-v1/selection" 17592186326270 "q-339239/mathematical-correction-v1/sele